Network administrators can create subnets using any other division that makes sense for the network.
Subnetting by Location
Network administrators can group devices according to their physical locations.For example, an organization can create separate subnets for different floors of a building.This helps organize the network according to where devices are physically located.

Subnetting by Group or Function
Devices can also be grouped according to their departments or functions.
For example, an organization may create separate subnets for:
Administration, Students, Human Resources, Accounting
This allows devices belonging to different departments to be organized into separate networks.

 Subnetting by Device Type
Network administrators can group devices according to their types.For example: Computers and other hosts.Printers.Servers.
This allows different categories of devices to operate within separate subnets.
